{"kind":"finding","id":"F-logistics-route-033-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/Logistics/LiveDeliveryMultiModuleTests.cs","line":138,"method":"UnloadedScan_MissingInventorySlots_FallsBackToNineSlots","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Logistics/LiveDeliveryCapacityProbe.cs:689-691; return 0 instead of slotCountFallback when InventorySlots is absent -> red","what_it_asserts":"With no persisted InventorySlots and all nine addresses pre-consumed, the scan returns -1 and reports consumedCount=9.","why_weak":"The name and comment claim the stock InventorySlots=9 fallback is pinned, but the 9 is the test's own slotCountFallback argument; ResolveUnloadedSlotCountFallback, which owns the stock default, is never called.","proposed_action":"Rename to UnloadedScan_MissingInventorySlots_UsesCallerFallback, and if the stock 9 is worth pinning, add a direct case over ResolveUnloadedSlotCountFallback (the sibling UnloadedScan_SmallerPrefabFallback_NoPhantomSlots already shows the parameter is caller-supplied).","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-logistics-route-033-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/Logistics/LiveDeliveryMultiModuleTests.cs","line":303,"method":"UnloadedStoredPartNode_AppendsWithoutDisturbingExisting","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Logistics/LiveDeliveryWriters.cs:490-491; stop overriding slotIndex in BuildUnloadedStoredPartNode -> red","what_it_asserts":"After adding a built STOREDPART node under an existing STOREDPARTS, both children are present with their own slotIndex and partName.","why_weak":"The appending the name claims is done by the test (ConfigNode.AddNode), not by the writer; WriteInventoryUnloaded (LiveDeliveryWriters.cs:413-432) is private and needs a live ProtoVessel, so no production append line is exercised and a clobbering append would stay green.","proposed_action":"Rename to reflect what is proven (BuildUnloadedStoredPartNode overrides slot and quantity on a copy) and record the append itself as in-game coverage alongside LogisticsDeliveryRuntimeTests, or expose the append over a ConfigNode seam so it can be driven headlessly.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"LiveDeliveryCapacityProbe","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/Logistics/LiveDeliveryCapacityProbe.cs","sut_line":561,"case_kind":"integration","proposed_name":"ProbeUnloadedFirstEmpty_FirstModuleFull_ReturnsSecondModuleSlot","sketch":"Extract the ProbeUnloadedFirstEmpty part/module walk into an internal pure helper over a list of (partIndex, moduleIndex, moduleValues ConfigNode) tuples, then drive two proto inventory modules where the first is full and assert the returned address is (1, m, firstFreeSlot).","guards":"The module-to-module handover, the persisted-vs-fallback slot-count choice at LiveDeliveryCapacityProbe.cs:583-585, and the early return at :591 have no headless coverage today; the existing unit test performs the handover itself, so a break-instead-of-continue regression in the walk would ship green.","risk":"career"}
